course: dictionary
lesson: 10744
title: Upward and upwards
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Upward means going up, towards a higher place. It can describe a movement, like smoke drifting upward, or a direction, like an upward slope. You can also use it for numbers: when prices go upward, they are getting higher.
explain: Look at the clues in «The wings bend upwards a lot in flight on purpose.» The word bend and the word flight tell you the wings are moving up, not down. Upward and upwards mean the same thing here.
explain: Upward is the opposite of downward. In maths, an upward movement adds to height, while a downward one takes it away. On a graph, an upward line shows that the amount is growing.
fact: Upward means going up, towards a higher place.
fact: Upward can also mean getting bigger or higher in number, like prices or temperature.
fact: «Upwards of» means more than, as in «upwards of 50 people».
fact: In science, hot air and smoke move upward, and plants grow upward towards the light.
fact: «Hatchetfish have eyes that point upwards to spot food falling from above.»
exercise: «Hot air and smoke move upward.» What does upward mean here? | Going sideways along the floor | *Going up, towards a higher place | Going down into the ground | Going round and round
exercise: In maths, what does an upward movement do to height? | *It adds to it | It makes it wobble | It takes it away | It leaves it exactly the same
exercise: «Hatchetfish have eyes that point upwards to spot food falling from above.» Find and copy one word that means in an up direction. | silver | hatchetfish | lights | *upwards
test: «A thunderstorm grows where warm, wet air shoots upwards into a tall cloud.» What does upwards mean here? | Staying still | Going sideways | Going under the ground | *Going up, towards a higher place
test: A line on a graph goes upward from left to right. What does it show? | The amount stays the same | *The amount is growing | The amount is shrinking | The line is broken
exam: Which phrase means more than, as in «upwards of 50 people»? | Look upward | Move upward | *Upwards of | Upward slope
